  "section_notes": "The final rules keep per-model results out of public view and set the S2 sales-stop limit at 10%, which protects the Hearth 10 (6.2%) but would not stop the Ember 8 (3.9%) on test grounds. S5 has no numeric mandatory recall: the 8/100k trigger only requires regulator notification and investigation, and recall depends on a regulator finding of unacceptable risk, which protects the Ember 8 (9.9/100k). S3 delays new-unit shut-off to 24 months, which is later than the 12-month acceptable benchmark, and S4's 36-month suppression deadline is within the acceptable range."
